think Design: the classic definition composes two erosions over structure.erode_se -- hit_or_miss(A) = erode(A, fg) AND erode(complement(A), bg). Compose not braid: this rung owns only the binarize (a pixel is shape when red >= 128) and the final AND (a per-channel min); structure.erode_se owns the fit gather; qoi owns the buffers.
think The alpha trap, seen before coding: a raw RGBA complement flips alpha 255->0, so a solid mask would erode to a transparent miss plane and the AND would zero it. The fix is to build both binary planes with alpha PINNED 255 (the background plane is the true set-complement without the transparency), so the output is clean opaque white-on-black.
obs GREEN on the first full metal run after one honest TEST-FIELD fix (not a code fix): the isolated dot at (3,3) had a 2x2 block whose corner (2,2) was a diagonal neighbor of the dot, so the dot was not truly isolated -- moved the block to the top-left corner clear of the dot's 8-neighborhood. Code was correct; the fixture was wrong (fixture-rather-than-remember, REDS pattern).
obs Proven: an isolated-point detector lights a lone dot and NOTHING else (lit count exactly one); the disjointness law (fg and bg sharing a cell -> all black, no pixel is both shape and ground); a background cell genuinely requires ground (a solid field matches nothing); the output opaque even from a translucent source; the 128 threshold (200 shape, 100 ground); QOI round-trip byte-for-byte; four refusals by name; determinism.
